From 32fc7c0facb0fcbfbaf0186ed5fe67e425a204d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 06:01:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/20] feat(deployment): number the deployment runs of a
 generation

Redeploying a service whose instance was lost needs a new deployment
run for the same generation: the run of that generation has already
succeeded, and its idempotency key (also the instance key) would hand
back the run and the instance that are gone.

deployment_run_key() takes an attempt number. The first attempt keeps
the key deployment:{uid}:{generation}, so runs started before this
change are found unchanged; later attempts append it, as in
deployment:{uid}:{generation}:{attempt}. find_deployment_runs() parses
the attempt and returns it with each run, so the release provider still
finds every run of a resource when it is deleted or redeployed.
